WEBVTT

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:07.590
<b>Toyo AUTO</b>

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:12.030
<b>Mitsuhoshi Bank</b>

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:12.030
<b>Izumo Naohiro</b>

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:12.030
<b>Kirishima Takuma</b>

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:11.290
Game and match won by Kirishima and Izumo.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:18.370
Aw, man. That wasn't even a warm-up.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.000
Kirishima.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.370
Takuma, Uni's playing SunBev.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.000
You're not gonna watch?

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.230
Nah, I'm sure my brother's 
team is gonna win anyway.

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:32.500
Isn't SunBev where Shiratori-kun went?

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.980
I heard he switched to doubles, too.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:36.240
Huh...

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.380
It'd be pretty interesting if they 
beat the world's second-best team.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.740
No one can do that except for Takkun.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.120
When's their match?

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:47.160
What? Ibuki-san, you're 
going to watch their match?

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.120
Yeah.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.820
<b>Sunlight Beverage</b>

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.820
(Player Name)

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.820
(Number)

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.820
<b>Shiratori Mikoto</b>

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.820
<b>Miyazumi Tatsuru</b>

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.820
<b>Saeki Sota</b>

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.820
<b>Saeki Toya</b>

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.820
<b>Takeda Koki</b>

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:54.210
Tatsuru...

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:59.280
<b>National Corporate Badminton Tournament Sixth Round
 Sunlight Beverage vs. Unisics</b>

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.250
Today's the day my racket spits fire!

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:06.380
Allow me to explain! If I imagine 
my opponents are naked...

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:09.000
Okay, okay! Let's try to chill out.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:10.470
We're going to win.

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:11.980
Yeah.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:19.880
Today's match is being broadcast, right?

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:21.650
Maybe we'll gain some followers.

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:23.120
Should we provide commentary?

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:24.430
Hype!

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:27.590
You two might not get the chance to play.

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:30.190
Hayato-san's team and I will get us two wins.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:30.770
Ow.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.730
Idiots, don't get ahead of yourselves.

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:35.610
You, too, Hayato.

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:38.690
Why am I getting yelled at, too?

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.560
There's no way I'd get ahead of myself.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:45.190
Not when they took a game 
off us the other day.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:49.430
It's nearly time. If we win this, 
we're in the semifinals!

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:52.250
But we're up against the powerful Unisics.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:54.210
It'll be a tough battle.

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:57.680
Wow, look at these people.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:01.130
It's been a while since I last 
watched a match. I'm excited.

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:10.360
You curious about your old team's match?

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:20.990
We'll be going all-out from the start today.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:25.240
<b><i>#07: Alternative</i></b>

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:38.720
First game won by Kirishima 
and Oginome of Unisics, 21-15.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.330
We lost.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:40.300
We haven't lost yet. We'll win the next one!

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:41.760
Right, Daddy?

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:43.820
I hope so.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:48.020
<i>Oginome's brilliant shots 
are forcing them to lob,</i>

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:50.390
<i>and Kirishima is smashing them down.</i>

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:53.140
<i>They're playing into their 
opponents' strategy.</i>

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:56.130
They're weaker than I expected.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:59.390
Why do you look mildly disappointed?

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:01.810
Let's win the next game.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:02.950
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:07.120
Those smashes are fast. I couldn't get them.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.580
We expected this.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:13.440
Just like we planned, 
it's time for Operation: Attack.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:14.670
That name...

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:21.610
Luck is on our side. The gym 
will favor us in the next game.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.770
Love all. Begin.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:32.730
<i>There it is.</i>

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:34.980
<i>It's low!</i>

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.280
What? You want to throw the first game?

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.870
We'll lay the groundwork to win the match.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:52.480
<b>A 7/19 Cross Hairpin</b>

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:52.880
<b>B 5/19 Hairpin</b>

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:52.880
For the first game, we'll let 
our opponents do what they want,

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:53.310
<b>Oginome</b>

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:55.830
<b>C 3/19 Push</b>

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:55.830
<b>Other 4/19</b>

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:55.830
<b>Straight 5/16</b>

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:55.830
<b>Cross 1/6</b>

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.830
and identify their habits and patterns.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:57.540
A-All right.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.830
Once they've let their guard 
down in the second game,

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:01.340
we'll answer their hairpin 
shots with attack lobs.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.020
Miyazumi-san's amazing!

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:16.480
<b>Miyazumi Tatsuru 
Shiratori Mikoto</b>

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:16.480
<b>Kirishima Hayato 
Oginome Daiki</b>

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:16.480
<i>I see. They're using attacking 
lobs to prevent me from smashing.</i>

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:17.820
Go!

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:19.300
<i>Here it comes!</i>

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:23.180
<i>I'm not hitting it over there.</i>

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:25.110
Yes!

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.070
<b>Miyazumi Tatsuru
 Shiratori Mikoto</b>

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.070
<b>Kirishima Hayato
 Oginome Daiki</b>

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:29.940
They're not too bad.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:31.540
No, but...

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:34.420
<i>In that case, I'll put some spin on 
my shots to catch them off-guard.</i>

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:39.130
<i>Even if they hit attack lobs,
 I'll force the smash!</i>

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.800
<i>They're not making this easy.</i>

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:55.060
<i>In this game, we've focused 
our shots on Kirishima Hayato.</i>

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:59.610
<i>They'll assume we'll do the same 
thing again, but we'll outwit them.</i>

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.530
One more point!

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:10.660
<i>All right, it's up in the air.</i>

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:13.910
<i>Perfect.</i>

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:17.540
<i>It's short?!</i>

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.590
<i>Is it the wind?</i>

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:21.300
<i>He realized too late.</i>

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.170
<i>Just as planned.</i>

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:26.500
The shuttle weighs five grams.

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:28.940
The slightest breeze affects its course.

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:32.530
Fortunately for us, 
we're playing upwind this game.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.020
Their shots will fall short.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:38.360
So that's what you meant when 
you said the gym would favor us.

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:42.330
If he smashes, you have to 
return it, no matter what.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.400
<i>Talk about an unreasonable request.</i>

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:46.900
It's out!

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:53.010
Yeah!

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:59.000
Second game and match won by Miyazumi 
and Shiratori of Sunlight Beverage.

00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:02.590
The world's number two team was beaten.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:04.170
Now they're even.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.300
It's down to the next game.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:10.820
<i>This time we're upwind!</i>

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:22.060
That went farther than I expected.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:27.150
<i>The previous game threw me off.</i>

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:29.610
<b>Miyazumi Tatsuru 
Shiratori Mikoto</b>

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:29.610
<b>Kirishima Hayato 
Oginome Daiki</b>

00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:35.170
<i>This is what we've been waiting for.</i>

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:37.130
<i>He just missed his smash.</i>

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:40.510
<i>A normal player would hesitate 
to aim for the same spot again.</i>

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:43.380
<i>But Kirishima Hayato, the perfectionist...</i>

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:45.070
<i>will go for this!</i>

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:47.690
Wow!

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:48.920
One more point!

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:06.110
<i>Come on, come on, come on!</i>

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:19.400
Yeah!

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:24.130
Game and match won by Miyazumi 
and Shiratori of Sunlight Beverage.

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:24.660
Yeah!

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:32.260
15-21, 21-19, 21-19.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:37.890
Now it's 1-1.

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:39.880
We'll win the next match, too.

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:43.770
You guys are amazing!

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:46.390
I can't believe you beat the 
world's second-ranked team.

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:47.490
Good work.

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:48.650
Thank you.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:51.110
You better ride this wave, bro!

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:53.070
Yeah.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:56.920
Sota-kun's opponent in the 
next match is Misora Ayato.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:08:00.730
Yeah. After winning the Inter-High, 
he joined a corporate team.

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:02.750
He's this tournament's youngest player.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.210
What kind of monster is he?

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.360
I look forward to our match, Elizabeth.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:15.840
Misora, don't do that during matches.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:17.450
Oh-kay.

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:20.820
He k-kissed it.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:21.810
Yeah.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:26.460
An eccentric pretty boy. I dig it!

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:27.390
One-love.

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:28.520
What, already?

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:34.380
<i>I'm coming for you, Elizabeth.</i>

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:37.950
<i>See? Gotcha.</i>

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:42.200
Yeah!

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:47.040
I know he's our opponent, but he 
makes me want to cheer for him.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:48.000
Yeah...

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:51.740
Just look at that. It's like he's 
playing around with the shuttle.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:55.270
Is it true that Sorarin can talk to shuttles?

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:57.600
I once saw him eating lunch with one.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:58.930
Huh?

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:04.010
You guys go get warmed up. 
We're gonna sweep this match.

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:04.980
Yes, sir!

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:12.730
Sota, up front!

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:15.610
<i>Close.</i>

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:21.660
Hey, when are you gonna
 actually start trying?

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:23.310
I already am.

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:24.890
Oh, really?

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:30.920
<i>I'm doing my best, too.</i>

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:34.110
A high backhand smash!

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:35.490
<i>But...</i>

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:40.560
<i>Some things just can't be done, 
no matter how hard you try.</i>

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:46.270
All right! That feels awesome!

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:50.960
Game and match won by Misora 
of Unisics, 21-14, 21-13.

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:57.880
Good work. That was a close game, Sota.

00:09:57.880 --> 00:10:01.160
Hardly. I don't stand a 
chance against a genius.

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:04.120
It's okay, Bro.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:07.660
We'll win the next game. Right, Ko-san?

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:09.790
Sure. You can count on us.

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:18.550
<i>We lost the other day, 
but I'm different today!</i>

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:31.650
Yeah!

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:39.700
<b>Takeda Koki 
Saeki Toya</b>

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:39.700
<b>Yagami Jun
 Natsuki Ryo</b>

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:42.080
Their movements have improved.

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:44.630
But we'll catch up in a sec!

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:46.160
Course we will!

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:50.330
<b>Takeda Koki 
Saeki Toya</b>

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:50.330
<b>Yagami Jun Natsuki Ryo</b>

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.070
Stick with it.

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:53.380
Roger that!

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:02.130
Did you hear? Kirishima Hayato lost.

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:06.080
I heard about that. His opponents 
were Miyazumi and Shiratori, right?

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:09.740
Yeah, that's it. Their team 
is... what was it again?

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:25.910
That's game. First game won by 
Yagami and Natsuki of Unisics.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:28.560
Did you see that super shot?

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:31.870
It was totally insane! There's our thumbnail.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:33.740
Sorry.

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:36.400
We couldn't help that. Let's get 
our heads in the next one.

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:44.260
Nice shot!

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.300
They're striking their signature poses!

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:47.920
Nice work, flashy boys!

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:56.480
<i>You have the showiness, cheeriness,</i>

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:58.940
<i>and freewheeling attitude 
to win over the audience.</i>

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:02.150
<i>That is your greatest weapon.</i>

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:04.290
<i>Make full use of it.</i>

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:08.870
<i>We're four points behind.</i>

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.050
<b>Takeda Koki 
Saeki Toya</b>

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.050
<b>Yagami Jun Natsuki Ryo</b>

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.050
Service over.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:13.750
<b>Takeda Koki 
Saeki Toya</b>

00:12:12.950 --> 00:12:14.460
<i>I'm not in bad shape.</i>

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:18.630
<i>I can see both our opponents 
and the court clearly, but...</i>

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:21.550
Service over.

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:25.280
<i>But I can't close this four-point gap.</i>

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:30.140
<i>I can't afford to lose.</i>

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:35.690
<i>For both the team's sake and my own...</i>

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:38.450
Hup!

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:42.150
<i>I have to give everything I've got!</i>

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:57.040
Game and match won by Yagami and 
Natsuki of Unisics, 21-16, 21-16.

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:53.250
Hell yeah!

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:02.410
Thank you.

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:05.290
That was a good match.

00:13:07.350 --> 00:13:10.220
<i>I can't believe they put up such 
a strong showing against Unisics.</i>

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:13.360
<i>They might actually be able to 
rank well at the next S/J League!</i>

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:15.810
Daddy.

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:19.400
Megumu has to pee. 
Could you wait for us at the exit?

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:20.370
Sure.

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:24.710
<i>I'm an idiot. What am
 I getting so excited for?</i>

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:36.800
<i>Now I get it. I'm jealous.</i>

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:44.830
<i>Reliable and stable. That's my motto.</i>

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.630
2. Marunaga Futami 496 Points

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.630
3. Hayashi Ken 495 Points

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.630
4. Hara Ryo 494 Points

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.630
5. Usuyama Toru 493 Points

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.630
6. Seki Hikari 490 Points

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.630
7. Furukawa Miki 489 Points

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.630
8. Ito Daisuke 488 Points

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:53.280
<i>Futami understands me better than anyone.</i>

00:13:58.490 --> 00:14:02.060
<i>I wanted to make her happy.</i>

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:12.660
<b>Maternity Record Book</b>

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:12.660
Guardian Name:

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:16.590
<i>Just before graduating from college, 
we learned she was pregnant and got married.</i>

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:19.830
<i>I quit playing badminton.</i>

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.130
<i>I'd protect my family.</i>

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.130
<i>That's all I was thinking about.</i>

00:14:27.390 --> 00:14:31.720
<i>Work, Futami, Megumu.</i>

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:35.650
<i>It's greedy to want</i>

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:39.750
<i>more than I already have.</i>

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:45.980
<b>Locker Room</b>

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:45.980
All right! We're gonna drink tonight.

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:49.500
The proposal's due first thing Monday, huh?

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:52.230
Has anyone seen my pants?

00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:53.070
No.

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:55.700
Why are you guys acting so normal?

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:59.740
There's no way you can be satisfied 
with only making it to the sixth round.

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:02.210
Hey...

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:05.750
Why do you care? You won.

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:08.740
Because we all have to win.

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:12.720
You know, because we're a team.

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:17.680
What's so funny?!

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:20.350
Just <i>who</i> said we're satisfied?

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:22.530
We all get it.

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:25.520
Acting glum about it won't change anything.

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:27.900
I'm glad to hear you say that, though.

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:30.380
You used to be so self-centered, but now...

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:34.510
"We all have to win because we're a team."

00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:37.360
What? Hey—

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:40.710
You've matured, Shiratori-kun.

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:53.130
Hey. We had some close matches, huh?

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:58.770
Not me. I can't keep up
 with a teen's stamina.

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:01.730
I see. Better get running, then.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:02.940
I suppose.

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:06.150
You've gotta practice if you want to win.

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:07.740
Excuse me.

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:08.500
Huh?

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:15.000
You're already so strong. 
What motivates you to try even harder?

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:23.210
There's someone I really don't 
want to lose to. That's all.

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:29.430
Are you okay?

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:35.270
Yeah, I'm fine. I just twisted it a little.

00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:36.930
Try to be careful.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:38.810
You're an old man.

00:16:39.670 --> 00:16:40.910
Excuse me.

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:43.020
No, excuse me.

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:46.480
You're Tatsuru's...

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:47.210
Huh?

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:51.110
I'm glad you found a nice partner.

00:16:51.770 --> 00:16:52.950
Izumo...

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:55.070
You two know each other?

00:16:56.560 --> 00:16:59.740
Izumo Naohiro. I'm Tatsuru's former partner.

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:00.710
Huh?

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:03.290
Well, if it isn't the loser.

00:17:04.660 --> 00:17:09.630
I heard you're playing doubles again 
after I crushed you at the Inter-High.

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:14.970
You deliberately went 
after Azuma, didn't you?

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:17.120
Crush the weaker player first.

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:18.570
It's standard practice.

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:23.040
Shouldn't you be worrying 
about your own team instead?

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:26.100
Our second-string team is 
still better than yours.

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:27.690
Takkun, let's go.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:31.570
Whatever. Good luck with 
your weak little team.

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:32.280
Hold on.

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:39.280
Kirishima Takuma, we'll beat you 
and Mitsuhoshi at the S/J League.

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:41.700
What? Who do you think you're—

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:42.690
Knock it off.

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:46.060
It's good to see you again.

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:48.180
Hello.

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:51.130
You can settle this on the court.

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:57.430
That said, beating Mitsuhoshi would 
make you the best in the world.

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:59.240
So good luck with that.

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:04.560
Take care of your leg.

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:19.450
Daddy!

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:22.160
Mommy said she won an award.

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:23.160
What?

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:24.870
<b>Arata Literary Award</b>

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:24.870
172nd Selection Results

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:24.870
<b>Winner "Ecstasy of the Dead" Yanagi Seiji</b>

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:24.870
<b>Winner "The Shepherd's Long Dream" Kigami Hana</b>

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:24.870
<b>Honorable Mention "A Single Human" Honda Minami</b>

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:24.870
<b>Honorable Mention "The Rain, the Sky, and 
Clouds of Dust" Usuyama Futami</b>

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:24.870
These 4 works have been awarded prizes
 A list of judges can be found below

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:27.370
That's amazing. Congratulations.

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:31.880
I'm one step closer to becoming an author.

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:36.590
It's because you helped me 
with housework and childcare.

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:38.630
I'll go for the grand prize next!

00:18:39.030 --> 00:18:39.670
Sure.

00:18:40.230 --> 00:18:46.000
Which means... you should
 play badminton again.

00:18:46.670 --> 00:18:47.950
You want to play with them,

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:50.570
don't you?

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:57.150
But...

00:18:57.450 --> 00:19:03.600
It's all right for us to have dreams even 
after we get married and become parents.

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:08.810
I might fail despite my efforts.

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:12.520
If that happens, Megumu 
and I will cheer you up.

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:16.310
Then you can look for a new dream.

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:17.630
Daddy.

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:23.640
<b>One Coupon to Play Badminton</b>

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:31.770
Thank you.

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:34.020
Come on, you'd better hurry.

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:37.070
I'll be back.

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.020
Go get 'em, Daddy!

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:43.360
Yeah!

00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:07.000
Wait! Wait for me!

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:10.000
Usuyama-san.

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:14.400
I run ten kilometers every day.

00:20:14.630 --> 00:20:16.420
I do strength training and 
practice my swing, too.

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:19.340
I'll pick up shuttles or do anything else!

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:24.160
Just please, let me play badminton!

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:30.650
It's been too long since you've 
played an actual match.

00:20:30.970 --> 00:20:33.520
You're not especially young, either.

00:20:35.340 --> 00:20:39.260
So you'd better play like 
your life depends on it.

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:40.960
You got that, Usuyama?

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:42.930
Yes, sir!

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:46.550
You made us wait long enough.

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:52.270
Out in the sixth round. That's how 
strong you guys are right now.

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:55.650
Based on that, I've gotta ask: 
how far do you want to go?

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:57.610
Winning the S/J League.

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:58.880
What other answer is there?

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:00.470
Wow, so confident.

00:21:00.470 --> 00:21:02.250
It's worth a shot.

00:21:02.250 --> 00:21:04.410
It'd be nice to win.

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:06.410
Let's go with that, then.

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:10.910
Then that's the team's goal.

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:13.660
We've got five months until the S/J League.

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:16.580
There isn't a moment to waste. Got it?!

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:17.570
Yes, sir!

00:22:56.360 --> 00:23:00.290
I see. So they lost.

00:23:03.780 --> 00:23:07.560
A weak team is a useless team.

00:23:08.170 --> 00:23:11.410
We must discard anything that's 
a burden to the company.
